    "description": "Original MCQs for a German firearms-expertise (Sachkunde, §7 WaffG) exam-prep module, covering the four AWaffV/WaffG-anchored knowledge areas required for the statutory Sachkundepruefung: (1) Grundlagen des Waffenrechts - basic concepts (what counts as a \"Waffe\"/\"Schusswaffe\", the permit-requirement/prohibition system, age limits, and the scope of the Sec. 7 WaffG expertise requirement, e.g. for security-guard and certain hunting/sport-shooting contexts); (2) Munition und Ballistik - ammunition components, caliber, ball vs. shot ammunition, expanding/hollow-point ammunition, caseless ammunition, and basic interior/exterior/terminal ballistics; (3) Aufbewahrung und Transport - the Sec. 36 WaffG safekeeping duty and its concretization in Sec. 13 AWaffV (DIN/EN 1143-1 security containers, ammunition storage, joint household storage, the pre-6 July 2017 VDMA 24992 grandfathering rule, storage in not-permanently-inhabited buildings, and practical transport/travel scenarios); and (4) Handhabung, Sicherheit und Handlungsrecht - safe-handling fundamentals (treat every weapon as loaded, muzzle discipline, unloading before disassembly, checking a handed-over weapon) plus the Sec. 32 StGB self-defense (Notwehr) framework as it is examined within the Sachkunde catalog (present unlawful attack, necessity/proportionality, warnings before firearm use, Notwehrexzess, and Putativnotwehr). IMPORTANT SCOPE NOTE: this module tests Sachkunde/knowledge content only for exam-prep purposes. It is NOT legal advice, does not replace a licensed Sachkundepruefung course or individual legal counsel, and must not be relied on for actual weapons-handling, storage, or self-defense decisions. Sourcing: the official Bundesverwaltungsamt (BVA) 'Fragenkatalog fuer die Sachkundepruefung (gemaess § 7 WaffG)' (Stand 16.12.2024, https://www.bva.bund.de/SharedDocs/Downloads/DE/Buerger/Ausweis-Dokumente-Recht/Waffenrecht/Sachkunde/Fragenkatalog_sachkunde_mitAntworten.pdf) was fetched directly and used as the primary structural/topical reference (its four core chapters map onto this module's four topics), together with the underlying WaffG, AWaffV, and StGB Sec. 32 statute text from gesetze-im-internet.de for legal citations. All question and answer text in this file is independently and originally phrased by the module author from the underlying facts and statute text - it is a synthetic reproduction, not a verbatim or at-scale paraphrase of the BVA catalog's exact question wording, consistent with this app's IP requirement for every module.",
